The Court identified four specific contingencies where a Writ Petition is maintainable, despite the availability of an alternative forum:
I. Where the writ petition has been filed for the enforcement of any of the Fundamental Rights;
II. Where there has been a violation of the principle of natural justice;
III. Where the order or proceedings are wholly without jurisdiction; or IV.
